smartinit.v3.3.1
November 2014 NAM smartinit Downscaling Bug fix

The primary change is to correct the diagnostic wind field model code to more accurately account for terrain effectfor the high resolution downscaled grids.

- Corrected wind downscaling error around coastlines
- Corrected wind downscaling error where winds were sometimes too strong near mountain ridge tops

Code Affected : sorc/smartinit.fd/
                - VADJUST.f90
                - NDFDgrid.f90
                - MAIN.f90
===================================================================================
1.  Wind downscaling error around coastlines

*   Moved vadjust call to come before coast-line correction code in NDFDgrid.f90

2.  Wind downscaling error near mountain ridge tops
===================================================================================

* VADJUST.f90:
A.  Scaling Factor
  - Implemented a scale factor, DSCALE, that reduces the terrain adjustment for winds 
    The adjustment is proportional to ratio of the difference of the model terrain and the NDFD 2.5 km terrain
  - DSCALE was further adjusted to not be greater than 1.0.
  - Slight adjustment for dscale subtracted model 1st level depth (H1) from HGHT to be comparable with ndfd terrain.
  - Terrain adjustment was turned off over water.

B. Terrain geopotential computation:

  - Switched back to use HBAR=HGHT (1) since it will never be less than 0 (death valley issue)


